"""Class-specific engineering notes; all behavior anchors are ArcCore 1.170 unslid VAs."""
NOTES={
'ArcAIDistilBertClassifier': '''This is configuration/value transport, not a classifier execution entry point in the reviewed methods. The five-argument initializer converts four strings, substitutes empty strings for nil, stores numClasses narrowed to short, and engages optional storage (0x443a46c). Getters expose string fields and signed 16-bit class count (0x443a764, 0x443a794, 0x443a7c4, 0x443a7f4, 0x443a824). mutableAIDistilBertClassifier exposes self+8 only when engaged (0x443a450). Native copy and cleanup helpers are 0x443a9fc and 0x42a4a04 as reached by 0x443a6f0/0x443a89c; their full semantics were not traced. No callback/queue contract is established. Replacement work is preserving value conversion, optional presence and narrowing; actual model-loading service behavior remains outside this class review.''',
'ArcAccessibilityActionData': '''Two initializers store an action code after a four-value range check (0x43deae8, 0x43deb44); an optional string is engaged only for non-nil input in the value initializer. value deliberately collapses absent and empty string to nil (0x43dec58). actionData copies action plus optional string rather than returning an ObjC object (0x43decac); metadata supplies the aggregate ABI. Cleanup releases long-string storage (0x43ded20). No callback or thread rule was established. Action meanings and conversion to actual accessibility actions remain unresolved; preserving an integer signature alone would miss nil/empty behavior.''',
'ArcAccessibilityTreeNode': '''The wrapper stores an inline native snapshot copied at initialization through 0x441daa0 (0x443ab2c), and converts native strings through 0x1c391bc for role/name/value/description/child-tree ID (0x443ab84, 0x443aba8, 0x443abcc, 0x443abf0, 0x443ac14). children returns boxed integer IDs, not recursively wrapped nodes (0x443ac38). Copy/access/destruction helpers are reached by 0x443acec, 0x443acf8 and 0x443ad04. No observation subscription or refresh mechanism was established here. A replacement must preserve snapshot fields and child-tree identifiers; integration with the live accessibility tree and update thread needs the producer's contract.''',
'ArcAutocompleteMatch': '''Initialization retains a native shared handle in an optional (0x4438b70), with cleanup at 0x4439d80. Most fields read native state and convert URLs or UTF-16 strings (for example 0x4438c94, 0x4438f9c). additionalData constructs an ObjC array of key/value records (0x4439348); duplicates lazily constructs/caches ArcAutocompleteMatch wrappers, and associatedKeyword wraps an optional associated match (0x44398c8, 0x4439ba8). No callback thread or native-match mutation policy is established. ArcBrowser consumes the native accessor for deletion (0x43e21d8). Chromium's AutocompleteMatch data is a source-backed comparison, not a proven binary type match: components/omnibox/browser/autocomplete_match.h:867,898,980,1083,1090. CEF navigation primitives do not by themselves reproduce ranking/provider/deletion semantics; API availability was not exhaustively audited here.''',
'ArcBackForwardList': '''Initialization retains native optional shared state and materializes backList/forwardList plus adjacent/current ArcBackForwardListItem wrappers (0x43df76c). The five ObjC getters are field reads (0x2d0fb40, 0x2cb140, 0x4084dc0, 0x4060580, 0x133ae90); infer their types from this class's metadata, not shared Ghidra names. Destruction releases native handle and ObjC fields (0x43dfc10). The native setter changes native optional state (0x43dfaf0); refreshing the materialized ObjC arrays is not shown there. No callbacks/queue were established. History navigation consumes a native item through ArcWebContentsNavigationController at 0x44180d4. CEF GetNavigationEntries (include/cef_browser.h:669) is a candidate for history enumeration, but snapshot identity/order and go-to-item parity need testing.''',
'ArcBookmarkTreeNode': '''Initialization and destruction retain/release an optional shared native handle (0x43dfd40, 0x43df69c); node accessors share an IMP with unrelated wrappers but retain their own metadata types. isValid dispatches to 0x42affa0 (0x43e05ac). liveChildren obtains current children through 0x42b00f4, creates wrappers and returns a copied array (0x43e05dc). IDs, UUID, parent ID and URL/title fields convert native values (0x43dfed8, 0x43dffa0, 0x43e0068, 0x43e01bc, 0x43e02d0). Ownership of the underlying bookmark model and validity after deletion remain open. No thread guarantee was established. Chrome bookmark-service integration is an implementation candidate, but these wrappers alone do not identify the precise service or establish a CEF route.''',
'ArcBrowser': '''This is an ownership and Chrome-service bridge. Init stores an optional shared native Browser, creates side-panel and creation-parameter wrappers (0x43e0c34); destruction releases those fields and delegate/native control blocks (0x43e320c). setDelegate builds weak delegate/self references or updates/clears the existing bridge (0x43e1284). Raw vtable prefix 0xda87798 links callbacks 0x43e33c4 (browser:didCreateNewWebContents:isActive:), 0x43e3458 (browser:didRestoreWebContents:withSessionId:), and extension-popup/action callbacks 0x43e3514, 0x43e35d4, 0x43e367c, 0x43e370c. This is a bounded prefix, not the full delegate protocol.

createWebContents passes native configuration through 0x42faa84, whose Arc browser_impl.cc path and tab/navigation creation calls establish a browser-layer route (0x43e154c → 0x42faa84). setWindow reaches platform association 0x43c8b18 through 0x42fa9fc (0x43e14d4); that helper keeps the initial association when already set, but the exact platform pointer/NSWindow/NSView contract still needs ABI review. takeOwnershipOfWebContents is a separate path with browser-liveness failure (0x43e1734 → 0x437b014).

Close completion is retained and queued in the native browser bridge; skip-before-unload affects native unload handling (0x43e1190 → 0x42fa5c8). Cookies, autocomplete, extensions, and session restore use distinct service bridges (0x43e18cc, 0x43e1f80, 0x43e23c0, 0x43e2b9c). 0x42fbd80 contains browser-deinitialized/unknown-keyword failures and captures incremental autocomplete completion. Exact invocation threads and teardown races remain unresolved. CEF supports browser creation/navigation (include/cef_browser.h:301,82), but its macOS parent_view forces Alloy (include/internal/cef_types_mac.h:110-153). Matching this native embedding contract plus Chrome service dependencies is a route gate; no drop-in CEF parity is claimed.''',
'ArcBrowserApplication': '''The ObjC application wrapper obtains a shared native application, creates LocalState, and registers a bridge with weak self (0x43e6548). init forwards nil to init: (0x43e6538); initialize: converts/copies config and returns native integer status (0x43e6fc8). run reaches native main-loop/shutdown orchestration (0x43e6ec0 → 0x42b1ba8), while tryToTerminate: retains completion and native code defers repeated termination requests (0x43e6ee0 → 0x42b2430). Destruction releases native/delegate pointers and ObjC caches (0x43eae38); this does not establish when global Chromium shutdown completes.

Weak histogram and accessibility observer captures are explicit (0x43e69a8, 0x43e6d80). Adapters send periodicHistogramSamplesAvailable: (0x43eb534) and accessibilityModeChanged: (0x43eb730). Breadcrumb/crash callbacks retain blocks (0x43e6b88, 0x43e6c84); their queue and unregister race remain unknown. createBrowser/popupBrowser wrap native Browser and set delegate (0x43e7048, 0x43e7528). Profile creation checks type 0/1 and bridges immediate NSError plus a retained completion; native bridge rejects empty names/null callback (0x43e8368 → 0x42b3d74). Profile deletion (0x43e8b58) and restoration with two callbacks (0x43ea810) require deeper durability/order checks.

Tracing/network wrappers are lazy caches (0x43e7b94, 0x43e7ea4). Service access includes flags, encryption availability/key export, enterprise device ID and imports; the matrix marks unresolved backend semantics instead of inventing ownership. No credential or live profile was accessed. Four pristine-app BL instructions were independently checked in evidence/app-launch-calls.tsv (app VAs 0x1004aa8c8, 0x1004ad74c, 0x1004ad770, 0x1004ad77c). Their receiver association is older-app pseudocode inference, not runtime class proof. Declared methods and direct call evidence remain separate. CEF primitive browser creation cannot establish parity for native application/profile/Chrome services; lifecycle and service parity remain route gates.''',
'ArcBrowserApplicationDebugProperty': '''The native DebugProperty contains two inline C++ strings according to ivar metadata. Initialization and setter copy both strings (0x43e6224, 0x43e6408); name/value convert each via 0x1c391bc (0x43e632c, 0x43e6350), and destruction frees long-string storage (0x43e64e4). The native property getter copies into return storage (0x43e6374). Producer is ArcBrowserApplication debugProperties, which constructs these wrappers (0x43e8f44). No callbacks, live binding, or sequence requirement was established. A replacement can marshal two strings but must identify the debug-property producer keys and values before claiming diagnostic parity.''',
'ArcBrowserContextDevTools': '''Base metadata declares six methods; Extensions adds isEqual: and hash with distinct method identities and no same-selector base override. Initialization retains optional native DevTools shared state (0x4437200); webContents reads native +0x98 and returns nil or an ArcWebContents wrapper (0x4437348). close conditionally calls 0xc107cd4 with mode 3, but Ghidra mistakes its ABI for C close(int) (0x4437324); recheck arm64 arguments before implementing. Extensions equality/hash use extracted native identity rather than ObjC wrapper address (0x43f8f28, 0x43f91fc). Cleanup shares 0x43df69c. No thread/close-completion contract is established. DevTools frontend hosting and context identity are the route questions; no CEF frontend/Chrome DevTools parity is inferred from method names.''',
'ArcBrowserCreateParams': '''The ObjC wrapper retains optional native shared creation parameters (0x4400f58, 0x43df69c). Native capability bytes back canResize/canMaximize/canFullscreen at native +0xa8/+0xa9/+0xaa (0x44010a4, 0x44010bc, 0x44010d4); initial bounds convert four integers to CGRect doubles (0x44010ec). initialOriginSpecified is native enum ==1 (0x4401118); pipSize traps when nested optional is absent (0x4401138), with an unusual second offset requiring ABI/disassembly confirmation. ArcBrowser constructs this wrapper (0x43e0c34). No callbacks or thread guarantee was established. CEF bounds/parent-view fields are comparison points (include/internal/cef_types_mac.h:100,110), but no mapping of resizing/fullscreen/PiP ownership is established.''',
'ArcColor4f': '''Stores four floats inline and copies 16 bytes in init/accessor/setter (0x443b1c8, 0x443b214, 0x443b220). Channel getters read +8/+0xc/+0x10/+0x14 (0x43dee04, 0x43dee0c, 0xc7fdb4, 0x43dee14). The Init category independently adds initWithR:g:b:a:, packing four floats then forwarding (0x4401b90). Both C++ lifecycle methods share a no-op IMP (0x15ac0). Ghidra also erases r's return entirely: pristine `ldr s0,[x0,#8]; ret` at 0x43dee04 recovers it (evidence/arm64-leaves.json). Ghidra's color4f return-register reconstruction is degraded; retain the metadata aggregate encoding and confirm arm64 HFA conventions. No callbacks/thread dependency or color-space/range/clamping semantics were established. This is value marshalling; no browser-service route is needed for the reviewed operations.''',
'ArcCommandBarRankingTensor': '''Inline optional native tensor stores name, integer dimensions and float payload. Init converts shape NSNumber values with intValue and data via 0x443181c (0x4431cec); shape/data allocate boxed numeric arrays (0x4432208, 0x44322c8). Native copy and cleanup reach 0x42a5760/0x42a44a8 (0x4432164, 0x44323e4); mutableCommandBarRankingTensor exposes engaged storage (0x4431cd0). No inference execution, callback or thread contract was established in these methods. Replacement must preserve element widths and array ordering; consistency of shape product versus data length, narrowing and consumers of tensor memory remain open.''',
'ArcConfirmInfobar': '''Initialization retains optional native ConfirmInfobar with a vtable-bearing value (0x443b22c); cleanup releases its shared control block (0x443b4a8). messageText converts native UTF-16 through 0x430dbcc/0x1d9fb90 (0x443b368). accept checks engagement and calls backend vtable +0x108 if live; Ghidra incorrectly uses socket accept's C ABI (0x443b434). Callback consumption, infobar dismissal and exactly-once acceptance remain unresolved. No queue affinity was proven. Chrome infobar integration or a CEF-specific emulation needs a confirmed delegate/action contract; the message getter alone cannot specify it.''',
'ArcDevToolsConnectionDialog': '''Inline native dialog holds three callback transports, corresponding to accept/deny/disable (0x4402950, 0x440296c, 0x4402988). Each checks a cancellation flag before indirect invocation. init/setter copy via 0x4335ae8; getter copies via 0x43359c8 (0x44028f8, 0x44029b0, 0x44029a4), while destructor tears down each callback transport (0x44029bc). accept has a false C socket prototype in Ghidra: preserve metadata ABI and verify actual registers. No proof was found that any action consumes all three callbacks or guarantees single use. Persisted-disable scope, callback thread, cancellation and reentrancy are consequential unresolved requirements for remote-debugging permission UI.''',
'ArcDownloadItem': '''Init retains optional native shared item (0x442f548), with shared destructor 0x440a40c; methods require optional engagement and check a live backend through virtual dispatch. completedBytes returns zero when backend is missing (0x442f66c). currentState maps native 0..3 to exposed 1..4, returning 0 for no live item (0x442fc60). remainingTimeInSeconds returns -1 on status failure (0x442fcd0). pause/cancel/resume/remove dispatch through native vtable slots, including forwarding cancel's boolean (0x442fd80, 0x442fdd8, 0x442fe38, 0x442fe90). Underlying download survival after profile shutdown, callback update producer and thread affinity are not established.

Chromium components/download/public/common/download_item.h:198-215,272,481-502 supplies source-backed candidate methods for these operations, not a proven vtable layout match. CEF feasibility requires preserving item identity/lifetime, state mapping, destination path and webContents association (0x442fa70); primitive download controls alone do not establish parity.''',
'ArcErrorStatus': '''An eight-byte inline native value is copied in initialization/getter/setter (0x443ba3c, 0x443ba90, 0x443ba9c); two 32-bit fields back processTerminationStatus and crashedErrorCode (0x443ba88, 0x189a538). Lifecycle IMP 0x15ac0 is shared no-op. Ghidra misrepresents aggregate return state at 0x443ba90, so metadata remains the ABI anchor. No callbacks/queue or ownership of external resources were established. Preserve value bits and independently resolve status/error enums at the producer; names alone cannot define crash handling.''',
'ArcFreezingVoteToken': '''This is move-owned native state: initialization moves a unique_ptr into self+8 and clears the input pointer (0x443eb10). clearVote calls 0x4335e08 only for non-null engaged token; that helper clears vote/liveness references and unregisters from a collection (0x443eb94 → 0x4335e08). Destruction clears pointer, calls 0x43363b4 and frees allocation (0x443ebb0). freezing_vote_token returns the address of wrapper storage, not a new owned token (0x283ebf0). Which performance-manager vote policy/sequence is involved remains unresolved; a generic browser freeze API cannot be assumed equivalent. Repeated clearing and destruction after graph shutdown are critical validation cases.''',
'ArcHistoryItem': '''Init retains optional native HistoryItem shared handle (0x442dfd8); cleanup/accessor share 0x43df69c/0x43df53c. historyID is formatted via 0xc248b4; URLs/title convert native strings (0x442e0fc, 0x442e1a0, 0x442e250, 0x442e318). Counts read native fields (0x442e3d8, 0x442e3f0). lastVisitTime converts native microsecond Windows epoch with saturation/special handling (epoch identification is source-backed inference from base/time/time.h:537-546 and the literal offset); visitTime can be absent (0x442e408, 0x442e4a8). No callback or thread policy was established. A history query producer and persistence semantics are outside this value wrapper, so neither Chrome-history identity nor CEF service parity is claimed.''',
'ArcHtmlToMarkdownResult': '''Initialization copies body/title/references/selectorsApplied/metaTags and stores percentage double (0x43dd5d4). Getter IMP aliases must be interpreted with this class's layout: +8 body, +0x10 title, +0x18 references, +0x20 selectorsApplied, +0x28 percentage, +0x30 metaTags (0x43dd450, 0x420b5f8, 0x420cb48, 0x41615f8, 0x416804c, 0x420c3e0). Destructor clears five ObjC fields (0x43dd740). Copy does not prove deep copy of collection elements. No conversion engine, callback or thread guarantee is shown here. Preserve schema and nil/copy behavior; the HTML extraction/Markdown producer remains a separate route question.''',
'ArcImage': '''Native image init/copy/destruction use shared image representation storage (0x440494c, 0x4404a7c, 0x4405068). nsImage converts through 0x2a02ccc (0x4404fec); isNull checks representation state (0x440500c). Class methods have separate + identity. dangerouslyDecodeFromData:scale: is a synchronous-looking native decoder bridge over NSData bytes/length (0x4404ad4 → 0x4337b04). Full decode retains completion and forwards dimensions/maxDecodedBytes (0x4404e6c → 0x4338920 → 0x4337e00). Short decode shares IMP with ArcImageRep and supplies three zero limits (0x4404fd0). Decoder helper closure, pixel formats, resource limits, NSData backing-buffer lifetime and callback queue remain unresolved. UI image identity and scale conversion need validation independently of the browser backend.''',
'ArcKeyboardAccelerator': '''Init calls NSObject init and stores native accelerator fields (0x4405fc8). key and modifiers share raw field-load IMPs with unrelated classes: self+8 and self+0x10 respectively (0x2d0fb40, 0x2cb140). This class metadata determines their actual scalar encodings, not Ghidra's ID return type. No owned ObjC field cleanup, callbacks or thread semantics were established. Key enum and modifier-mask conversion at menu/keyboard consumers remain the route questions; these methods alone do not define native event synthesis.''',
'ArcMemoryDumpProvider': '''initWithName:dataProvider: retains block and creates native RAII provider (0x44077b4 → 0x432b4b8). Bridge prefixes provider name with bcny- and checks runtime state; identification of TLS/task-runner-looking state as the registration task runner is a source-backed inference. Callback adapter 0x4407b5c creates a completion block around the native dump callback and invokes the ObjC provider block. dealloc clears owned pointer, unregisters/destroys provider and then calls super; .cxx_destruct has a second null-guarded cleanup path (0x4407a04, 0x4407ac4). Do not translate both into unconditional duplicate destruction.

Candidate source identification is MemoryDumpManager registration/unregistration, supported by lifecycle shape and pinned base/trace_event/memory_dump_manager.h:80-106: manager does not own provider; task runner determines callback affinity. This source comparison does not prove which registration overload/sequence Arc uses. Outstanding completion lifetime, destruction sequence and whether callback can arrive after dealloc remain unresolved. A CEF route would need separate diagnostics integration; no public API-absence claim is made.''',
'ArcMenuModel': '''Init retains optional native shared menu; items lazily materializes/caches ArcMenuItemModel wrappers from 0x432c5e4 (0x4440638, 0x444075c). Shared destructor releases cached ObjC collection and native handle (0x440a40c). menuWillShow/Close indirectly dispatch slots +0x100/+0x108 (0x4440a3c, 0x4440a5c). Their identification with ui::MenuModel hooks is a source-backed inference from pinned ui/base/models/menu_model.h:222,226 and call context; the binary vtable type has not been independently resolved. No callbacks/queue contract or item-cache invalidation was established. A replacement must preserve show/close lifecycle and dynamic-item changes, not only enumerate a static menu.''',
'ArcNomicEmbedTextItem': '''Two native C++ strings represent text and task; init converts nil inputs to empty strings (0x442d568). Native-copy init copies both strings (0x442d6f8); getters convert them through 0x1c391bc (0x442d10c, 0x442d7fc), and native getter/destructor share IMPs with PasteAndGoClassification because layouts match (0x442d150, 0x442d244). Metadata preserves distinct aggregate identities. mutableNomicEmbedTextItem returns engaged storage address (0x442d54c). No model execution, callbacks or threading policy was established. The engineering task here is value marshalling and lifetime; embedding task vocabulary and inference service are separate questions.''',
'ArcNotification': '''Init retains optional native Notification handle (0x4408b0c); 0x440a40c releases native state and cached iconURL. id and browserContextQualifiedID are distinct selectors sharing the same string getter IMP 0x4408d64; do not invent different semantics from names. items/buttons construct ObjC snapshots, including text-input button flags (0x44094bc, 0x4409688), while category builds action/category objects through deeper native/platform helpers (0x4409d38). didReceiveResponse delegates to a platform-response adapter with close/settings/click handlers (0x440a1f8); didClose/click/settings reach native notification callbacks 0x433edd0, 0x433ee60, 0x433ef10 through 0x440a0fc, 0x440a114, 0x440a1e4. The response parser and notification-center ownership, action identifiers and callback thread remain unresolved. Browser context association is wrapped at 0x44092d4. CEF route viability needs native macOS notification/action parity, not only web Notification rendering.''',
'ArcNotificationButton': '''Stored fields title/icon/placeholder are returned from +0x10/+0x18/+0x20 (0x2cb140, 0x4084dc0, 0x4060580). Setters use objc_storeStrong, not copy (0x420b588, 0x4401164, 0x4408ac4); isTextInput is scalar +8 (0x40b1230, 0x43e0930). Destructor clears three object fields (0x4408ad0). ArcNotification creates/fills these wrappers in buttons (0x4409688). No callback/queue contract was established. Preserve this data transport and distinguish mutable object retention from copy; platform action parsing remains in the notification class.''',
'ArcOverscrollBehavior': '''init calls NSObject init then stores both directional values as 0 (0x440a7b4). x/y are scalar loads at +8/+0x10 and setters directly replace them (0x2d0fb40, 0x2cb140, 0x440a7f0, 0x416803c). Shared IMP Ghidra names/types are not this class's API types. No callbacks, persistence or thread policy was established. Meaning of enum 0 and conversion to renderer/native overscroll policy must be recovered at the consuming method; no CEF mapping is asserted from these scalar fields.''',
'ArcOverscrollParams': '''init allocates ArcOverscrollBehavior and stores it strongly (0x440a7f8). Getter/setter/destructor access/replace/release the object field at +8 (0x2d0fb40, 0x43eae2c, 0x4166068). This retains the supplied behavior object, with no copy shown. No callbacks or thread policy was established. The consuming web-contents/renderer bridge, enum meanings and effect of mutating the shared behavior after application remain open route questions.''',
'ArcPasteAndGoClassification': '''Native optional value contains two C++ strings, copied in init (0x442d008) and destroyed at 0x442d244. menuTitle converts first string (0x442d10c); destinationURL passes second to URL converter 0x43abd34 (0x442d13c). Native getter shares IMP/type-recovery artifacts with NomicEmbedTextItem but metadata encodings remain separate (0x442d150). This wrapper does not classify input in the reviewed methods. No callback/thread contract was established. Locate the classification producer and URL normalization/error policy before choosing Chrome omnibox integration or CEF-side emulation.''',
'ArcSelectOption': '''Inline optional native SelectOption stores two optional strings and two booleans. Init uses native copy helper 0x83694e8 and destructor frees long-string storage (0x442bee4, 0x442c1e8). value/text return nil for absent native string, while present empty strings pass through string conversion (0x442bf94, 0x442c084); optional wrapper itself must be engaged. isSelected/isDisabled read +0x48/+0x49 with engagement guard (0x442c174, 0x442c188). No callbacks or thread guarantee was established. Select-control identity, action routing and popup ownership must be found at producer/consumer; this class specifies only option transport.''',
'ArcSessionTab': '''Init retains optional native SessionTab shared handle (0x443cb9c); navigation array is cached ObjC state at +8 (0x443cde8). setCurrentNavigationIndex traps for negative/out-of-range index (0x443ccf8). setNavigations stores supplied array strongly, extracts native navigation handles and replaces native vector through 0x4340c10 (0x443d0c8); current-index adjustment was not established. groupId returns nil if absent or uppercase 128-bit hex string (0x443d7b4). lastActiveTime converts Windows-epoch microseconds with special values (source-backed epoch inference from base/time/time.h:537-546 and literal offset) (0x443cd44). Pinned components/sessions/core/session_types.h:44-49,77,86,100 provides a source-backed SessionTab comparison, not verified layout equivalence. Persistence is not implemented by this wrapper; foreign-tab restore consumes it in ArcBrowser 0x43e2c10. CEF history enumeration alone does not establish session metadata/restore parity. Threading and native-session cache invalidation remain open.''',
'ArcTabGroupInfo': '''Initializer establishes defaults and an ObjC tab-session-ID collection (0x43e0970); groupId/title/tabSessionIds setters use nonatomic copy (0x43e0938, 0x43e09fc, 0x43e0a0c), while extensionGroupId/color/collapsed are scalar fields (0x43e09f4, 0x43e0a04, 0x43e0930). Destructor releases stored collections/strings (0x43e0a14). Shared field-load IMPs have different scalar/object types on other classes; this metadata is authoritative. No callback/queue or persistence was established. Replacement needs producer-defined defaults, color enum and session-ID ordering; live Chrome tab-group service integration remains outside this value class.''',
'ArcTabGroupResult': '''Initializer calls NSObject init and establishes scalar defaults (0x43e08e4). success and extensionGroupId are direct scalar fields; error/groupId setters use nonatomic copy (0x43e0930, 0x4168044, 0x43e0938, 0x420b594). Destructor clears two ObjC string fields (0x43e0940). It transports operation result rather than exposing a callback implementation in the reviewed methods. No threading rule was established. Error-string vocabulary and native/extension group-ID correspondence must come from the producer before implementing tab-group command parity.''',
'ArcWebContentsAIAgent': '''Init retains optional native shared agent handle and cleanup releases it (0x4440a7c, 0x43df69c). sendTextInput converts text and reaches a macOS native-view path (0x4440ba0 → 0x4354de4 → 0x473dff4); the last helper iterates NSString code units, synthesizes NSEvent key events and sends keyDown:. sendKeyPress similarly reaches enum-selected synthetic event (0x4440c34 → 0x4354ea0 → 0x473e20c). It is not established as a CDP or renderer-Mojo method. Weak native-view references are handled in the bridge. No dispatch to main/UI thread was established; native AppKit operation alone is not proof caller affinity is enforced. Exact key enum, surrogate/IME behavior, focus, modifiers/keyCode and view lifetime are critical. CEF would need compatible native event/hosting behavior; public key injection existence would not prove this contract.''',
'ArcWebContentsConfiguration': '''Inline native config supplies direct flag bytes; constructor zeroes flags but sets initiallyHidden true (0x4414cb0). Getters/setters touch packed fields; forced size is optional int32 width/height converted to CGSize or CGSizeZero (0x4414bf0). Small/nonpositive dimensions clear it; conversion guard traps on some out-of-range inputs (0x4414c18), with NaN and rounding requiring instruction confirmation. nativeWebContentsConfiguration/setter copy packed bytes (0x4414c88, 0x4414c9c); .cxx_destruct is no-op (0xfbc0). ArcBrowser createWebContents consumes this value (0x43e154c → 0x42faa84). No callbacks/queue rule is shown. Hidden/foreground/background, PDF, downloads, autoplay and context-menu flags need consumer tracing to establish actual enforcement. CEF macOS hidden/parent_view fields (include/internal/cef_types_mac.h:105-153) are candidate comparisons, not a complete mapping.''',
'ArcWebContentsNavigationController': '''Native controller is optional shared state at +0x10 with weak owner +8 and a vector of shared observer bridges (metadata; 0x4416bec, 0x43fe218, 0x44191d8). Init's by-value native/owner arguments are mis-split by Ghidra; use metadata and verify registers. addObserver deduplicates by pointer, creates weak observer/owner bridge and registers (0x4416eac → 0x4333598); removeObserver unregisters then erases/releases, with absent observer a no-op (0x4417210 → 0x4333650). Raw bridge vtable 0xda882d0 links provisional callback 0x44193c0, which wraps ArcNavigation and sends webContents:didStartProvisionalNavigation:. Four distinct later targets lack exact indexed bodies (0x44195b4, 0x44197a8, 0x441999c, 0x4419b90); their semantics are unresolved.

Short load supplies transition=1/fromAddressBar=true/typedWithHttpScheme=false (0x4417484); full load normalizes transition and returns ArcNavigation or nil on bridge failure (0x441749c → 0x4366ac0). The bridge validates destination and initiator origin, detects cleared web contents, and has separate Chrome browser-tab and standalone-webcontents branches. Back/forward/go-to-item/reload wrap native navigation result (0x44179dc, 0x4417d58, 0x44180d4, 0x441853c, 0x44188bc). Reload bridge maps bypass mode to enum 2/check-for-repost true (0x43680fc).

Pinned content/public/browser/navigation_controller.h:565-592,647-692 and page transition/reload enum headers provide source-backed comparisons, not exact binary identifications. CEF provides GoBack/GoForward/Reload/ReloadIgnoreCache (include/cef_browser.h:82-118), but those void commands do not directly implement ArcNavigation object identity and observer ordering. Callback queue, cancellation, stale history items, same-document events and post-removal delivery need behavioral tests. Parent-view forcing Alloy (include/internal/cef_types_mac.h:151) remains relevant when combining navigation with Chrome services.''',
}
